# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audius developer API key.
#
# Get one at https://audius.org/developers (Developer Apps -> create an app).
# Audius documents the API key as safe for frontend/browser use, so it is
# exposed through Vite's VITE_ prefix on purpose.
#
# NEVER put an Audius bearer token, API secret, or private key in a VITE_
# variable: everything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the public bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_AUDIUS_API_KEY=

# Name reported to Audius for API usage attribution. Optional.
VITE_AUDIUS_APP_NAME=Pulse Music Platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER ONLY — never expose to the browser.
#
# Jamendo client id, from https://devportal.jamendo.com.
#
# There is deliberately NO `VITE_JAMENDO_CLIENT_ID`. Jamendo's developer terms
# treat the client id as a personal credential that must not be disclosed, and
# any variable prefixed VITE_ is compiled verbatim into the public JavaScript
# bundle. The browser therefore never sees this value: it calls the same-origin
# route /api/jamendo, and the serverless function injects the credential
# server-side (agents/16_JAMENDO_SERVERLESS_SECURITY.md).
#
# Leaving it blank is a supported state: Jamendo is simply unavailable and the
# application keeps working on the Audius catalogue alone.
#
# Local development reads this from .env / .env.local through the Vite dev
# middleware; production reads it from the Vercel project's environment
# variables, where it should be marked sensitive.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
JAMENDO_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER ONLY — never expose to the browser.
#
# YouTube Data API v3 key, from the Google Cloud console. See the "YouTube
# fallback" section of README.md for the full step-by-step, in short:
#
#   1. create (or pick) a project at https://console.cloud.google.com
#   2. enable "YouTube Data API v3" for it
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#   4. Edit the key -> API restrictions -> Restrict key -> YouTube Data API v3
#   5. paste it below (locally) and add it as a Vercel environment variable
#      marked Sensitive (production)
#
# There is deliberately NO `VITE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY`. Anything prefixed VITE_ is
# compiled verbatim into the public JavaScript bundle, and a Google API key in
# the public bundle is a key anyone can spend against your daily quota. The
# browser therefore never sees this value: it calls the same-origin route
# /api/youtube, and the serverless function injects the credential server-side
# (agents/23_YOUTUBE_SERVERLESS_SECURITY.md).
#
# Leaving it blank is a supported state: the YouTube fallback simply disappears
# from the UI and Audius + Jamendo keep working exactly as before.
#
# Quota note: a new project gets 100 search.list calls PER DAY for the whole
# deployment. That is why YouTube only ever runs on an explicit click.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
